# data/raw/ is scratch: yfinance/screener.in caches, run logs, and
# superseded pilot outputs - all large and/or regenerable by re-running
# the relevant script against cached or live sources (see docs/decisions
# and scripts/*.py for how). data/processed/ holds point-in-time
# snapshots of the outputs actually worth keeping (full universe
# fundamentals, final pilot/backtest results, the two section 7 charts)
# copied out of data/raw/ deliberately - not auto-tracked, so a
# regenerated data/raw/ file doesn't silently change committed history.
data/raw/
data/cache/

